Welcome to the Proteus Internet Doorway.


I am much better at programming than writing docs, so bear with me
if I omit something.

Unpacking:

Unpack Proteus.lha anywhere you like, here is where the files go:

	1. Make a directory called 'PID' in the Pfiles:
	2. Put everything in 'Pfiles:PID'
	

Setup:

Setting up Proteus depends on the following to be true:

 {You have C-Net set up}
 {You have installed AmiTCP 3.0 (or better) and it works}
 {You have installed InetUtils 1.3 (or better)}

If these are done, the proceed with the following, if not, set up the
above and get back to this later.

	1. Edit PIDfig for your site. It is commented and should be
	   apparent as to what things do.
	2. Adopt Proteus, Pedit, Pdir as pfiles

Thats basicly all there is to it!


Functional Overviews:

Clients:

	Clients like ftp, telnet, archie, and ncftp all have support
in Proteus, there is a menu system built in that allows users to
easily access services and ftp sites.

	FTPD: There is ftpd support as well, specificly for M.Saunby's
FTPD server, which is just about released.

	IRC: Sorry, there is no irc client that works in a cli
enviroment yet, the only on i know about works in a damn window so is
useless to all bbs's.

AmiTCP support:

	Proteus will automagicly add new users into the system with a
minimum of fuss.  It will create the personal directory for each user
in the dir you specified with the FDIR parameter in PIDfig.  Proteus
also sets up a .plan file for finger support and each user is also
placed in the passwd file for AmiTCP with the proper variables in
place as well.  Proteus will route all ftp 'GET's to the users
personal dir as well.  Proteus fully suports the ncftp .netrc file and
allows users to change it with the Pedit program.

Archie:

	Archie has full functionality in Proteus with is own menu and
revolving choices.  The ability to send results to yourself via mail
or plunking it right in your personal dir is invaluable.


Other: 

	Other clients like ping are supported and such.  New clients
that WORK will be added in the future as they are created.



Menu file structure and other files:

All menus in Proteus except the ftp and telnet menus have defaults.
You can override these by creating the proper menus with these names:

	MAIN.mnu	- this is your main menu
	EDIT.mnu	- this is your main menu for Pedit
	UDIR.mnu	- this is your main menu for Pdir


Other files used in Proteus include:

	NEWS.txt	- A general news file read to users at login
                          to Proteus
	longtime.txt	- A file to explain time delays in Archie


telnet and ftp menu file structure:

file called FTP.mnu contains catagories for submenus.
the structure s simple:

-----------8<-------------------
Amiga FTP sites
IBM ftp sites
Adult FTP sites
.
.
.
Misc FTP sites
-----------8<-------------------


As you see, each line is a menu choice, and the position of the line
corresponds with which menu is chosen, so the first line will choose
the menu called FTP.1, the second line will choose FTP.2 and so forth.

Now the actual FTP.# files contain actual info on sites that people
choose off of a list.  Each FTP.# file may contain up to 50 entries

the format is as follows:

--------------8<-----------------
ftp.nisc.sri.com			< line 1, actual address  <---
New User's Questions 			< line 2, One line comment   |
Hitchhikers Guide			< line 3, misc comment       |
Gold in Networks!			< line 4, misc comment       |
The above can be found at this ftp site < line 5, misc comment       |
ftp.cs.widener.edu		<-this starts a new record,  ---------
Zen & Art of Internet
goto the pub/zen/ for this file


csn.org
Zen ASCII version
Look in pub/net/zen/ for this


hydra.uwo.ca
Guide Internet/Bitnet
look in libsoft/guide1.txt


--------------8<----------------

As you see, each record consists of 5 lines, the first is the address,
the second is the onle line comment displayed to users, and the rest
are displayed to users when they choose this site.  The next record
starts on the line after the last one.  You must use blank lines for
comment fields that are empty!

I have included my sample files for you to modify or expand on. 




